{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-01 is satisfied on all four limbs, so the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee is legitimately chargeable. Limb (a): EV-TRIP-02718 carries a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-08-13T20:36:57+08:00. Limb (b): EV-GPS-02718 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from that same timestamp, the first qualifying in-geofence fix. Limb (c): the continuous in-geofence dwell is 181 seconds, past the 180-second free waiting period in force. Limb (d): no boarding event is recorded and the trip was terminated by the driver at 20:39:58 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes that limb recognises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02718", "EV-GPS-02718"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival geofence test of POL-NS-02 is met with room to spare: the driver's track shows 19 consecutive qualifying in-radius fixes, running from 20:36:57 to 20:39:58, against the clause's requirement of at least 3 consecutive fixes. The trip record's 'arrived' event at 20:36:57 coincides exactly with the first of those fixes, so the arrival is established by live geofence entry and not by the button tap alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02718", "EV-TRIP-02718"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The measured dwell exceeds the required minimum, so POL-NS-06 refunds nothing. The longest qualifying run is 181 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period in force for this STANDARD-class trip under trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec (the record carries platform_policy, so resolution_rule reads 180, not the retained pre-version-2 table figure). The shortfall is -1.0 seconds, that is, a surplus. POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the 'arrived' tap, which is exactly the 181-second run recorded here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02718", "EV-TRIP-02718"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival marker is not false, so POL-NS-05 does not fire and no false-arrival referral arises. POL-NS-05 catches a marker made more than 300 m from the pin, or at 15 km/h or above. Here the driver's first in-geofence qualifying fix begins the dwell run at exactly the marker timestamp, with a dwell_start_offset_sec of 0.0, so the marker and the recomputed clock coincide rather than diverge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02718", "EV-TRIP-02718"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-03 does not reach this trip. That clause applies only where the driver is stationary for the required dwell at a point OUTSIDE the POL-NS-02 arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin. Here the 19 qualifying stationary fixes are inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, so there is no wrong-entrance or wrong-face case, and no refund route opens under this clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02718", "EV-TRIP-02718"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider. Limb (a) fails because the chat log EV-CHAT-02718 contains exactly one message and it was sent by the driver, not the rider, so no rider locating or coordinating message exists in the waiting window; limb (b) is therefore never reached. Limb (c) is not merely undecidable but affirmatively failed: all 41 of the rider's fixes in EV-GPS-02718 lie between 874.8 m and 880.9 m from the pickup pin, and rider_qualifying_fix_count is 0 against a 100 m STANDARD rider_presence_radius_m. The rider's device was nowhere near the pickup point for the whole window.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02718", "EV-GPS-02718", "EV-TRIP-02718"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver did more than wait: 20 seconds after his arrival marker he sent the rider an in-app message at 20:37:17 reading 'im at the pickup point', delivered at 20:37:18 and read by the rider at 20:37:47, some 131 seconds before he cancelled. The record shows no reply from the rider and no movement of the rider's device toward the pin; the sole chat message in the bundle is the driver's own notice.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02718", "EV-TRIP-02718"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "null",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's counterparty statement - 'I waited the free period then cancelled' - is corroborated by the telemetry rather than merely asserted. The free waiting period of 180 seconds is recorded as started at 20:36:59 in EV-TRIP-02718, and EV-GPS-02718 independently shows the driver holding position inside the geofence for 181 seconds from 20:36:57 until the cancellation at 20:39:58.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02718", "EV-GPS-02718"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's claim that the driver 'cancelled almost immediately' is refuted by the record it is filed against. The driver accepted at 20:32:01, ran 4.9 minutes to the pickup, marked arrival at 20:36:57, and cancelled at 20:39:58 - 181 seconds of in-geofence waiting measured from his first qualifying fix and 179 seconds after the platform's own free-waiting timer started. A charge of SGD 4.50 on that sequence is the fee the rider paid for the waiting period, and the waiting period was served.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02718", "EV-GPS-02718"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout. All four POL-NS-01 conditions hold and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces them, so the driver is compensated at 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee in force for this trip, that is SGD 3.60, the residual 20 percent being retained as the platform service fee. The fee itself stands as charged and the outcome the case produces is DRIVER_COMPENSATION.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02718", "EV-TRIP-02718"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip, so compensation is paid rather than withheld and no escalation follows from that limb. The check requires BOTH driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d at 4 or more AND that counter over driver_profile.completed_trips_30d above 0.08. EV-DPROF-02718 shows 0 terminations in 30 days against 62 completed trips 30 days, so neither limb of the check is met.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02718"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "null",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is present on this record. Limb (c) cannot fire: rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0. Limb (d)'s abuse test needs rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d at 3 or more and it is 1, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip. No two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence, and no deciding fact rests on impaired evidence because every artifact in the bundle is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02718", "EV-DPROF-02718", "EV-GPS-02718"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "null",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The money block is clean and there is no POL-NS-08(d) integrity defect. fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee of SGD 4.50 equals trip_record.platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of SGD 4.50 and is the net figure produced by resolution_rule for this trip, so the ledger reconciles to total_charged. Every artifact the driver relies on - EV-TRIP-02718, EV-GPS-02718, EV-CHAT-02718, EV-FARE-02718 and EV-DPROF-02718 - carries admissibility status COMPLETE and weight_multiplier 1.0, so nothing in this brief is down-weighted and no disclosure under POL-GEN-02(1) is owed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02718", "EV-TRIP-02718"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.difference",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

